        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy the dock if you have <strong class="text-white">a shedding pet, children, a large home or allergies</strong> — in those houses the small onboard bin is the constraint that limits how useful the robot is, and removing it changes the machine entirely.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Skip it for a <strong class="text-white">small pet-free apartment</strong>, or if the budget forces a choice between the dock and better obstacle avoidance — <strong class="text-white">navigation decides whether the robot cleans at all</strong>, and that is the more important problem to solve first.
          </p>
        </div>

